{
    "type": "game",
    "name": "A Deep World",
    "steam_appid": 3290130,
    "required_age": 0,
    "is_free": true,
    "controller_support": "full",
    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3290130/extras/1498d2b81aec3eed1284bb0a3ff7b3f9.avif?t=1754911681\" data-has-big width=800 height=132 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A Deep World is a 2D stealth adventure game set in an alien underwater realm. Guide a fragile little creature as it explores, hides, and outmaneuver procedural animated monstrous predators on it quest to rescue a lost friend!</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Features:</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Dynamic Underwater World</strong></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Explore a mysterious, alien ocean teeming with life and danger, all possible thanks to procedural animations, and stunning 2D art.</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Minimalist Stealth Gameplay</strong></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Outsmart procedural animated predators by sneaking, hiding, and using your wits and sound to survive, but be careful! Making sounds might distract a predator, might lure them to you, or might open something who knows.</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>A cinematic emotional journey</strong></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Embark on a heartfelt adventure to reunite with your lost companion and find your way back home. All told through animation and sound. No HUD, no dialogue, no pop ups.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >About the development</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A Deep World was originally created as project in a game design graduate class at USC Games, in collaboration with students from Berklee School of Music. Later finished and polished for this full release by Jose Striedinger.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3290130/extras/1498d2b81aec3eed1284bb0a3ff7b3f9.avif?t=1754911681\" data-has-big width=800 height=132 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A Deep World is a 2D stealth adventure game set in an alien underwater realm. Guide a fragile little creature as it explores, hides, and outmaneuver procedural animated monstrous predators on it quest to rescue a lost friend!</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Features:</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Dynamic Underwater World</strong></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Explore a mysterious, alien ocean teeming with life and danger, all possible thanks to procedural animations, and stunning 2D art.</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Minimalist Stealth Gameplay</strong></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Outsmart procedural animated predators by sneaking, hiding, and using your wits and sound to survive, but be careful! Making sounds might distract a predator, might lure them to you, or might open something who knows.</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>A cinematic emotional journey</strong></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Embark on a heartfelt adventure to reunite with your lost companion and find your way back home. All told through animation and sound. No HUD, no dialogue, no pop ups.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >About the development</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A Deep World was originally created as project in a game design graduate class at USC Games, in collaboration with students from Berklee School of Music. Later finished and polished for this full release by Jose Striedinger.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>",
    "short_description": "Guide a little green creature as it goes deep into a dark, dangerous underwater world once sealed off. You'll need to explore, hide, and outmaneuver different predators to find your lost friend and make it back home in one piece. Whatever you do, avoid the nests!",
